OPA Task--

Implementation Summary

Implemented and tested key Zero-Trust security components in the Kubernetes zt-integration namespace.

Completed work:

Deployed OPA and Envoy alongside a demo application.

Configured OPA authorization policies with JWT-based role validation.

Tested authorized and unauthorized requests.

Configured frontend and backend workloads with certificate-based mutual TLS (mTLS).

Verified successful TLS authentication and rejection of requests without client certificates.

Implemented Kubernetes NetworkPolicy to allow backend access only from authorized frontend workloads.

Verified that unauthorized pods are blocked while authorized frontend-to-backend communication continues successfully.

Test Results:

Unauthorized request without a valid JWT: HTTP 403.

Authorized guest GET request: HTTP 200.

Restricted guest POST request: HTTP 403.

Successful frontend-to-backend mTLS: HTTP 200.

Missing client certificate: HTTP 400.

Unauthorized pod network access: Connection timeout.

Authorized frontend access after NetworkPolicy: HTTP 200.

Note: The current workload mTLS implementation uses classical RSA certificates and X25519 key exchange. Post-quantum hybrid key exchange is maintained as a separate demonstration and is not yet integrated into this live workload mTLS connection.

Environment: Windows 11, Minikube, Kubernetes, OPA, Envoy, OpenSSL and PowerShell.
